Sync-time instrument - mm20 investigation opener.

Every llama_decode on the CVM carries a model-size-independent fixed cost
of ~5-8 ms (2026-08-03 measurements: 1-layer MTP head decodes 8-12 ms,
65-layer batch-1 15.4 ms where graph exec accounts for ~10, batch-5 verify
30 ms where exec accounts for ~24). That constant is what makes sequential
draft steps unprofitable and holds plain decode at ~62 tok/s. The prime
suspect is cudaStreamSynchronize under SEV-SNP - the CC host<->device
round trip. This patch times every stream sync in ggml-cuda cumulatively
and exports ggml_backend_cuda_sync_stats() (C symbol, dlsym'd by the
enclave shim - no link-time dependency, CPU flavors unaffected). If the
fleet shows sync_us/token in the multi-ms range, the follow-up is a
doorbell completion path (graph's tail node writes a pinned flag the host
spin-reads) - a candidate +20-30% on EVERY decode mode.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
index a7f2bf7..201c4f1 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
@@ -94,6 +94,29 @@ static_assert(sizeof(half) == sizeof(ggml_fp16_t), "wrong fp16 size");
 #define GGML_LOG_WARN_ONCE(str) \
     { static std::once_flag warn_flag; std::call_once(warn_flag, []() { GGML_LOG_WARN(str); }); }
 
+// enclave sync-instr (mm20 investigation): cumulative wall time spent
+// INSIDE stream synchronization. Every decode on the CVM carries a
+// model-size-independent ~5-8 ms fixed cost (measured 2026-08-03: 1-layer
+// head decodes 8-12 ms, 65-layer batch-1 15.4, verify b5 30) and the CC
+// host<->device round trip on sync is the prime suspect. The counter names
+// it: sync_us / decode ~= the tax, directly. Exported C symbol so the
+// enclave shim can dlsym it from the dlopened module (no link-time dep).
+static std::atomic<int64_t> g_enclave_sync_us{0};
+static std::atomic<int64_t> g_enclave_sync_calls{0};
+static cudaError_t enclave_timed_sync(cudaStream_t s) {
+    const int64_t t0 = ggml_time_us();
+    const cudaError_t e = cudaStreamSynchronize(s);
+    g_enclave_sync_us.fetch_add(ggml_time_us() - t0, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    g_enclave_sync_calls.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    return e;
+}
+extern "C" int64_t ggml_backend_cuda_sync_stats(int64_t * calls) {
+    if (calls) {
+        *calls = g_enclave_sync_calls.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    }
+    return g_enclave_sync_us.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+}
+
